cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or method, please cite the manuscript below."
title: "module-aging-toolkit: a single-cell framework with built-in controls for module- and cell-type-resolved transcriptomic clocks"
abstract: >-
  Code, result tables, figures and verification script for the manuscript "Can transcriptomic clocks
  be read by module and cell type? Validated controls and a demonstration in pulmonary fibrosis".
  Version 0.3.0 (Zenodo DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23306962) corresponds to the revised manuscript that uses
  the serialized module clocks. Version 0.2.0 retrained those clocks and is withdrawn.
  Version 0.1.0 is the original submission.
  The toolkit's own code is MIT-licensed; third_party/tage_prep.py is derived from Materials
  distributed under the MGB Open Access License 1.0 and is restricted to non-commercial academic
  use (see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).
